Falsifies `virtio::verification::the_directory_lookup_is_total`.

The defect: the entry is sliced by index, `&directory[at..at + ENTRY_LEN]`, in place of
`directory.get(..)?`. The two read the same on a whole directory block, and only a directory cut
short, or a header whose count claims more entries than the bytes hold, tells them apart. Those are
exactly the bytes a hostile or damaged disk hands the driver.

Expected to fail: the slice's bounds check, on a directory length that ends inside an entry the
count still names. The driver would panic on a block it read from the device rather than report
the file missing.

diff --git a/crates/virtio/src/lib.rs b/crates/virtio/src/lib.rs
--- a/crates/virtio/src/lib.rs
+++ b/crates/virtio/src/lib.rs
@@ -527,3 +527,3 @@ fn find_file(directory: &[u8], name: &[u8]) -> Option<u32> {
         let at = nifefs::HEADER_LEN + i * nifefs::ENTRY_LEN;
-        let entry = directory.get(at..at + nifefs::ENTRY_LEN)?;
+        let entry = &directory[at..at + nifefs::ENTRY_LEN];
         let field = &entry[..nifefs::NAME_LEN];
